{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Fund well-maintained bleed kits in places where young people live/learn & travel",
        "additional_details": "A person can bleed to death within minutes. In a serious bleeding emergency, the period before an ambulance arrives can be critical.  We are not asking for bleed-control kits to replace prevention, policing, first aid or ambulance services. It is simply an additional layer of life saving protection.\r\n \r\nPreventing violence matters - but when an injury happens, saving the life in front of you matters too. The kits can be used for any bleed emergency so benefit the community as a whole",
        "background": "Calling on the Government to introduce a fully funded national programme providing accessible bleed kits in places where young people spend their time.\r\nLocations should include:\r\nSecondary schools; higher education & Uni\r\nCommunity centres\r\nSports grounds & leisure facilities\r\nMajor transport hubs",
